  // 29.4 s with a 663-character answer), but every hop had JRN_TIMEOUT_MS (12 s), so the abort cut the stream after the 200 arrived and the
  // journey read "http 200, 0 events". The ask hop gets JRN_ASK_TIMEOUT_MS, and a stream cut by the timeout is reported as one.
